 "markdown": "md/cancers/UCEC.md",
 "notes": [
  "The selected analysis panel is one selection for one study design. General availability per TCGA project is reported separately and is larger; do not mix the two.",
  "Spatial studies come from patients other than those in TCGA. They add tissue context, not measurements for TCGA patients.",
  "Spatial resources are shown at two image levels. \"Original H&E located\": the original scan, measured expression and coordinates were found. \"Matched data with preview image\": expression and coordinates match a released preview image, and the original scan was not located; such data support molecular spatial maps, not whole-slide or tile models, cell morphology, physical distances or registration sign-off. Registration, calibration and tissue QC may be pending at either level.",
  "Spatial section records are per study, not globally unique physical sections or independent assays. Patients are study-local IDs given by the source; sections without one add no patients, and no eligible-patient total is established.",
  "Counts reported by a study keep that study's own unit (sections, slides, samples, donors) and are never added across studies. An unknown count is absent, not zero.",
  "located_sections lists selection fields only; the full record with links, source wording and clinical fields is in data/captures.json under the same id."
 ],
 "cancer": {
  "code": "UCEC",
  "gaps": [
   "Histology comes from the TCGA endometrial study where the case is in its table and from the GDC label otherwise: 398 endometrioid, 112 serous, 12 mixed and one other among the 523 selected patients. These are analysis annotations, not independently reviewed current diagnoses.",
   "Nineteen cases have a publication histology that differs from the GDC label; both are kept.",
   "The endometrioid-only subset (398 patients, 303 with both assays) is a sensitivity analysis within the cohort, not a separate cohort. No smaller serous cohort is selected.",
   "Histological type and the published molecular groups (POLE, MSI, copy-number low and high) do not coincide; a molecular serous-like or endometrioid-like profile is not a reason to exclude a case. Uterine carcinosarcoma (TCGA-UCS) is not added.",
   "Some retained patients have RNA-seq without 450k methylation, and some normal-reference patients have no retained primary-tumour assay.",
   "Two endometrial spatial resources are listed for review: one primary-tumour Visium sample, and four metastasis biopsy sections from two donors before and during NP137 treatment, for exploratory treated comparison only. None is yet a verified matched package."
  ],
  "name": "Uterine corpus endometrial carcinoma",
  "group": "tcga-panel",
  "hausser": "no-geometry",
  "strata": [],
  "summary": "Hausser et al. screened this cancer type and detected no significant archetype geometry in their RNA representation. It meets the molecular screen and is analysed as one pooled endometrial carcinoma cohort, with reviewed histology, grade and the published molecular groups kept as annotations and an endometrioid-only sensitivity subset.",
  "tcga_project": "UCEC",
  "analysis_cohort": "UCEC"
 },
